10.11.549.491 D Parsed message: {"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"client_outcome\": \"unknown\",\n  \"client_refs\": [],\n  \"contexts\": [\n    \"sensor_action_not_client_result\",\n    \"rule_match_not_intrusion_proof\",\n    \"comparison_incomplete\"\n  ],\n  \"delivery_complete\": false,\n  \"intrusion_established\": false,\n  \"next_checks\": [\n    \"correlate_client_receipt\"\n  ]\n}","reasoning_content":"We have a synthetic SOC evidence. The user wants me to analyze it and return exactly a six-field JSON object.\n\nLet's parse the evidence:\n\n- coverage: current_retained_records: 15, omitted_groups: 0, prior_window_available: false, retained_window_complete: false, udp_delivery_complete: false.\n- groups: 1 group with count 15, all fields listed.\n- original_records: 15 records, all with same fields.\n- permits: client outcomes, context codes, etc.\n- receipts: empty array.\n- untrusted_annotations: one annotation.\n\nKey observations:\n1. This is a synthetic fixture. It says \"Constructed offline fixture, no captured network traffic.\" There are no actual network receipts.\n2. The \"original_records\" have 15 entries, all with identical content. They have event_utc, protocol, source_alias, source_port, destination_alias, destination_port.\n3. The \"groups\" has 1 group, all records in the group have the same event_utc, etc.\n4. Receipts array is empty.\n5. There is no client_result receipt. No process_socket receipt.\n\nThe task is to perform SOC evidence analysis. The required fields are:\n- attempt_id\n- event_utc\n- protocol\n- source_alias\n- source_port\n- destination_alias\n- destination_port\n\nAll seven must be present and exactly equal on the same record.\n\nWe need to choose the client outcome before choosing checks.\n\nSince there is no matching client_result receipt (receipts is empty), the client_outcome is \"unknown, with client_refs []\".\n\nThe context decisions:\n- Always include coverage_limits because these inputs do not establish complete UDP delivery.\n- For nonempty evidence include sensor_action_not_client_result and rule_match_not_intrusion_proof.\n- For a matching client_result include client_receipt_scoped_to_attempt. (Not applicable here, as no matching client_result)\n- For a matching process_socket include process_receipt_not_client_result. (Not applicable here)\n- Include comparison_incomplete when retained coverage or the prior window is unavailable.\n- Include untrusted_log_text when an annotation actually instructs the analyst.\n- Empty evidence does not support sensor/rule contexts. Do not infer safety from an empty window.\n\nThe evidence is non-empty (15 records in groups and original_records). So we need to include sensor_action_not_client_result and rule_match_not_intrusion_proof.\n\nWait, we have no matching client_result. So client_outcome is \"unknown, with client_refs []\".\n\nAlso, we need to determine if intrusion_established is true or false. The source says \"Constructed offline fixture, no captured network traffic.\" The evidence is synthetic. The analysis says the packet was \"Constructed offline fixture\". The group and records all have the same fields. There is no actual network traffic. The intrusion_established should be false because there is no captured network traffic and no evidence of intrusion.\n\nThe delivery_complete should be false.\n\nThe context_code is \"comparison_incomplete\" because retained coverage is not complete (prior_window_available: false, retained_window_complete: false).\n\nWait, let's check the exact rules from the procedure.\n\nThe procedure says:\n- \"Choose one to three checks that resolve the remaining uncertainty.\"\n- \"Empty evidence or missing retained/prior coverage: inspect_coverage. With nonempty evidence and missing coverage, correlate_client_receipt is also useful if the client result remains unresolved.\"\n- \"Complete retained/prior coverage, no matched client or process receipt: correlate_client_receipt, correlate_proces